    "created_at": "2017-07-25T03:32:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-25T03:32:57Z",
    "body": "Current implementation of WebKit and Blink:\r\n\r\nFor now, ```FileList``` is a normal interface, not an Array. The ```files``` setter accepts only a ```FileList``` object, and never accepts Blobs.\r\nAn HTMLInputElement object retains the passed FileList objet, and ```files``` getter returns it as is.\r\n\r\n```\r\ninputFile2.files = inputFile1.files;\r\ninputFile2.files === inputFile1.files\r\n>>> true\r\ninputFile2.files[0] === inputFile1.files[0]\r\n>>> true\r\n```\r\n\r\nI also found Edge's ```files``` was settable.  In Edge, it seems the ```files``` setter does deep-copy.  i.e.\r\n\r\n```\r\ninputFile2.files = inputFile1.files;\r\ninputFile2.files === inputFile1.files\r\n>>> false\r\ninputFile2.files[0] === inputFile1.files[0]\r\n>>> false\r\n```\r\nBut Edge didn't accept a normal Array of ```File```s.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
