    "updated_at": "2017-12-04T02:10:30Z",
    "body": "From https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dnd.html#datatransfer\r\n>The DataTransfer() constructor, when invoked, must return a newly created DataTransfer object initialized as follows:\r\n>  \r\n>  1. Set the drag data store's item list to be an empty list.\r\n>\r\n>  2. Set the drag data store's mode to **read/write mode**.\r\n>\r\n>  3. Set the dropEffect and effectAllowed to \"none\".\r\n\r\nSince the *drag data*  from a DataTransfer instance created by the constructor is set to mode *read/write*, a script can set arbitrary files to a FileList object, and by extension to an `input[type=file]`.\r\n\r\nI may have misread [comment#5](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2861#issuecomment-317657810), but I thought this shouldn't be possible.   \r\n\r\nIf it is indeed intended to be possible, then the route to do it seems quite complicated, when such methods could be implemented directly on the FileList class.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
